    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="0737" n="731" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg731"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.48/2013a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State (Welles) to the Greek Minister (Diamantopoulos)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-07">January 7,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: I refer to your letter of
                    December 23 [<hi rendition="#italic">22</hi>] 1941, transmitting a communication
                    from His Excellency Emmanuel Tsouderos, Prime Minister of Greece, addressed to
                    the President, regarding the situation in Greece and the need for relief
                    supplies to be sent to that country. I also refer to your letter of December 24,
                    1941, in which you suggest that advantage be taken of the presence in the United
                    States of the British Prime Minister to discuss with him the question of the
                    relief of Greece.</p>
                <p>The communication from the Greek Prime Minister and a copy of your own letter
                    were placed before the President. Mr. Roosevelt has now requested me to transmit
                    to you, for forwarding to its high destination, his reply to Mr. Tsouderos’
                    communication. I have pleasure in enclosing the President’s response.<anchor
                        n="11" xml:id="d723-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d723-f1" n="11" xml:id="d723-f1-content">
                <p>Not attached to file copy, but see draft of letter from President Roosevelt to
